![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The `sourceArtifacts` parameter is accessed directly with `?.find` without ensuring it is an array. If `sourceArtifacts` is passed as a non-array or is malformed, it will throw a `TypeError`. Use `Array.isArray` to safely default to an empty array if the property is not an array, preventing TypeErrors.

```suggestion
  const requiredArtifactsLoaded = REQUIRED_SOURCE_ROLES.every((role) => {
    const artifactsList = Array.isArray(sourceArtifacts) ? sourceArtifacts : [];
    const artifact = artifactsList.find((item) => item.role === role);
    return artifact?.exists === true && artifact?.loaded === true;
  });
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When dereferencing and mapping properties from potentially missing or malformed input artifacts, use Array.isArray to safely default to an empty array if the property is not an array, preventing TypeErrors.
</details>

